+## 3. Test Plan
+
+### Preparation And Evidence Recording
+
+After approval and fresh bound dispatch, T-001 records the full commit ID, Node/runtime versions, approved source digests and relevant tracked/untracked baseline paths with content digests. Save the pre-implementation UI diff separately as baseline evidence; do not reset, squash, commit or retroactively attribute those earlier changes to this Run. Test fixture mutation stays in isolated temporary control repositories, never live neighboring Runs. Source evidence and final scoped diff must distinguish this increment from the baseline.
+
+Evidence files use the actual run-local path .agdf/control/artefacts/backlog-status-flow-clarity-20261009-01/evidence/. They record scenario IDs, commands, working directories, exit status, input/source/runtime versions, outcomes and gaps. Preserve existing proof files. Screenshots/traces are useful only when tied to the tested source and observation time; copy/link actual returned local evidence without fabricating a digest or a displayed result.
+
+### Automated Lanes
+
+Use the repository's verified Node 22-or-newer supported runtime; capture the actual version. Commands below are intended checks after their source/tasks exist, not already executed proof:
+
+1. Focused Core summary/codec checks: node packages/core/test/backlog-work-summary-test.js and node packages/core/test/backlog-summary-codec-test.js, when introduced. They exercise production owners and fixture state/failure matrices, not duplicated mapping logic.
+2. Dependent writes/revision/recovery: run existing packages/core/test/run-backlog-writer-test.js, run-step-transaction-test.js, artefact-recording-test.js, run-revision-test.js and run-source-revisions-test.js using node; run packages/cli/scripts/run-recovery-test.js plus the existing approval/relationship continuation test owner identified by T-001. Extend its real failure/confirmed-commit coverage rather than creating a substitute repair writer.
+3. Read/list/source behavior: node packages/core/test/control-cockpit-projection-test.js, cockpit-scoped-read-test.js, cockpit-list-test.js, cockpit-backlog-title-test.js and next-action-test.js, plus directly affected capture tests. Assert list file dependencies/bytes and zero persistent mutation.
+4. UI: npm --prefix packages/control-ui run typecheck; run focused Vitest files with its existing local executable for compact, scoped-reading, presentation/work-step, backlog titles and added summary cases. Run its existing node test/service.test.mjs where read envelope/HTTP behavior is affected. Broaden to the package test lane once the integrated source changes are ready; repeat only after new failures/corrections justify it.
+5. Browser: build the actual source with npm --prefix packages/control-ui run build and run build:mcp when validating the MCP resource. Use the existing Playwright test:browser lane focused on backlog.spec.mjs, backlog-titles.spec.mjs and scoped/journey cases that exercise direct summary/action and selected mismatch. Fix the asset digest/build under test via AGDF_COCKPIT_TEST_DIST when isolation is necessary. Wait for explicit request/response completion rather than networkidle because the service long-polls changes.
+6. MCP mediation: reuse packages/cli/scripts/cockpit-scoped-mcp-test.js/cockpit-mcp-test.js and the directly affected packages/mcp-server cockpit/protocol/continuation contract tests against the exact prepared source payload. Capture runtime/UI/resource binding and old-field fallback; do not assume a locally installed older server validates new source.
+7. Finish with git diff --check, relevant existing documentation/link validation and the applicable repository verification profile selected from the actual changed paths. Record per-lane scope. Build/profile preparation is evidence tooling, not permission to install, publish, release or change host configuration.
+
+The exact baseline/tool prerequisite and current test entry-point coverage are resolved during T-001 from actual repository code. Missing executable/dependency/fixture proof is an explicit owner-bound limitation; no silent skip or installation workaround. Do not weaken assertions or broaden governance scope merely to obtain green output.
+
+### Visible And Native Evidence
+
+T-007 records compact and expanded browser views at representative approximately 390px and 1200px reading widths, including the motivating QA-evidence row, a long action, old/unverified row and recoverable error. Exercise keyboard selection/source details, source mismatch, visible retry and delayed-title downward-scroll cases. Verify control bounds, row meaning, completed query, focus and scroll before/during/after loading; save evidence tied to the exact fixed build. UI inspection is read-only.
+
+For a claimed current native MCP App path, prepare the observation sequence first: identify fresh resource and exact runtime/UI digest, current Run/observation, expected compact/expanded row text, widths/scroll/error cases and evidence destination. Use only the supported already accessible host/resource mechanism. An expired view or old installed bundle cannot substantiate new behavior. Source/browser rendering, protocol text and successful build are separately labelled evidence. If fresh supported native display is unavailable, record the exact evidence obligation and required observation action; do not add an installer/profile/configuration change or close another Run's finding. qa-gate must not claim applicable native/UX evidence fulfilled while this remains missing.
+
+### Completion And Review
+
+T-008 records actual task/scenario status and the final change inventory without a parallel acceptance source. T-009 records implementation/test fulfillment through existing canonical owners, then performs mandatory Code Review plus Task Plan Review and Clean Implementation Review as evidence dimensions. Findings retain stable IDs and existing normalized gap types/routes; resolve code defects in authorized CD+Tests and obtain upstream revision/approval when requirements/design/plan materially change. qa-gate alone decides pass/revise/block. A pass is separate from exact human QA approval and later UAT/OR/closeout.
+
+## 4. Brownfield Scope
+
+The approved BROWNFIELD_REVIEW establishes the required structured_delivery route and medium UX impact with ready analysis. Before implementation the distinct pre_implementation_analysis checks actual owners and reuse against this approved TP: plain policy versus refinement, every row-construction/dependent write, exceptional recovery, consumed-source guards, immutable read/DTO paths, rendering and the dirty UI baseline. Persist BROWNFIELD_ANALYSIS.md through the existing owner and fresh gate routing. Do not silently treat the earlier sizing review as implementation preparation.
+
+Preparation may refine file-level implementation mechanics within these approved decisions. A new storage/authority/compatibility or recovery decision, missing product requirement or contradictory owner evidence routes to the existing earliest UR/PRD/SD/TP owner; it is not permission for a parallel store, gate or local workaround. Existing SOT registry, runtime contracts and architecture documents remain primary sources according to their declared boundaries. No memory/Context Graph node or approved source rewrite is part of execution.
+
+## 5. Out Of Scope
+
+No gate/policy/approval-order change, independent UI evaluator, second persistent control store, new generic subsystem or separate acceptance registry. No bulk backlog migration, list-wide Run/report scan, arbitrary reclassification/archive, automatic delivery continuation triggered by list reading, other Run's QA/finding closure, publication, release, installation/configuration/profile rollout, Git commit/push/PR or multi-host qualification. Earlier opt-out UI fixes are baseline, not retroactively governed changes or evidence that the new increment works. Do not modify approved UR/PRD/SD or sealed historical proof files to force plan fulfillment.
+
+## 6. Risks And Blockers
+
+| Risk / missing proof | Required treatment | Existing owner / exit condition |
+|---|---|---|
+| Sources, gate or intended Run change during execution | Stop dependent work and refresh binding; use supported revision/recovery when material | gate-check and affected source owner; exact valid current revision before continuation |
+| New helper changes allowed/forbidden/approval or QA authority | Block quality claim and repair within existing owner; upstream revision if intent/design changes | Core evaluation/code-review; unchanged authorization regression proven |
+| Source movement or marker/revision mismatch around commit | Revise implementation/evidence; preserve foreign updates/receipt history and existing pending recovery | Writer/transaction owner; passing real boundary/recovery scenarios |
+| Unsupported/ambiguous/oversized saved observation or skipped pointer | Expose safe limited state and explicit operation-specific repair; no false synchronized/current claim | Backlog/read owners; documented tested strict/skip/limit behavior |
+| Exceptional recovery is accidentally coupled to a second journal | Block unsafe design/implementation; preserve existing recovery owner | SD/Core recovery owner; actual journal/confirmed-commit tests and review |
+| Old labels/DTOs/layouts lose original meaning or section/search changes | Revise compatibility implementation; do not bulk rewrite historical rows | Existing backlog/read/UI owners; exact preservation and old-field fallback evidence |
+| Native current display unavailable or source/browser proof used as substitute | Keep applicable evidence obligation open; no QA pass/host-readability claim while unverified | Existing visible-evidence/qa-gate owners; fresh supported observation with exact identity |
+| Dirty UI baseline contaminates diff/evidence or adjacent Run artefacts change | Stop attribution/foreign work, preserve protected bytes and establish scoped increment | Preparation/review owners; BASELINE and actual final diff/source inventory agree |
+
+No material product or design question is deferred to implementation; execution details and actual evidence availability are T-001/T-007 obligations. An unfulfilled scenario is explicitly partial/missing/not_verifiable, not silently fulfilled by an unrelated green lane. Repeat only affected tests after changes and record the actual remaining gap.
+
+## 7. Next Step
+
+Validate this plan's criteria/decision/task/scenario mapping, localized summary and exact approved SD derivation, then canonically record it. Present for a new deliberate Approval: TP, revision or rejection. Valid approval permits required implementation-preparation Brownfield Analysis, followed by CD+Tests only when that evidence and fresh control route allow it. It does not approve QA/UAT, authorize VCS/installation/release or resolve another Run's findings.
