+
+Initial checks are not represented as pass: the first new component selector was ambiguous between summary and raw original; it was scoped to the visible strong summary. The pre-existing visibility test waited for a fetch invocation rather than the resulting stale disabled control and failed twice; its assertion now waits for that actual user state with no removed requirement. The isolated new browser fixture initially omitted required preparation paths/reasons, detected explicitly by Core assertions and corrected; Chromium initially required authorized execution outside the macOS sandbox. Final valid fixture and observable-state checks pass. A first package probe used the non-UI server profile; it was not activated and was replaced by the existing cockpit:true npm assembler in a separate profile. Neither failed package nor intermediate qualified profile was activated. The final reviewed profile is dist/local/backlog-summary-report-findings-verified-20261009/preparation.json.
